1|0@AirForce^1438673995#ctqvp7a:KiLLaHMoFo$:Definitely agree with what most are saying here. I was stationed at Travis for 4 years (the dorms aren't dry anymore?) and I actually enjoyed my time in the dorms. The chow hall was amazing, I met a ton of people in the summers when I would grill out, and I saved a bunch of money. It will make you appreciate living off base a lot more if you stick it out. As for getting married. Here's a little bit of advice from someone who almost took that route once too. Don't even CONSIDER getting married to someone until you have lived with them for a period of time and know that you can spend several days together without wanting to choke each other. Case in point: my ex fiancée and I were great for two years. No issues. I move off base when my time is up and she moves in with me only to find out she's a complete slob. Love doesn't do dishes. Love doesn't do laundry. Love doesn't pay bills. It's a realistic part of life. We split up two months after living together. 
